==========================================================================================
INVARIANT ALGEBRA under order-join T1|>T2  (verified on all class pairs, n1+n2<=7)
==========================================================================================
  c3(T1|>T2) = c3(T1)+c3(T2)   : True
  tr(T1|>T2) = tr(T1)+tr(T2)   : True
  scc(T1|>T2)= scc(T1)+scc(T2) : True
  H(T1|>T2)  = H(T1)*H(T2)     : True   (Redei-path count is join-MULTIPLICATIVE)

  strongly-connected iso classes (the join-atoms): n=3:1, n=4:1, n=5:6, n=6:35, n=7:353

==========================================================================================
COUPLING-LAW BATTERY  (predict via velocity/join, CONFIRM exhaustively over all 530 classes)
==========================================================================================
  srange <= tr             FAILS n=7    join-mono=False | inflation-FRAGILE via D- at n=6 (predicted by decoupling)
        witness: n=7 c3=4 H=15 tr=5 srange=6 smax=6 kings=1 dom=1
  c3 <= H                  HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  n - c3 <= tr             HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  tr <= smax + 1           HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  dom + tr <= n + 1        HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  H <= 2^(n-tr)            FAILS n=3    join-mono=True 
        witness: n=3 c3=1 H=3 tr=2 srange=0 smax=1 kings=3 dom=2
  H <= 2^(n-2)*c3 + 1      HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  kings <= 2*c3 + 1        HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  srange <= tr + c3        HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)
  srange <= 2*(tr-1)       HOLDS n<=7   join-mono=True  | join-monotone => REDUCES TO STRONG CORE (verified on cores)

